{title: Welcome, Happy Morning}
{artist: Venantius Fortunatus, tr. John Ellerton / Arthur S. Sullivan}
{genre: Easter}
{style: Anthem}
{flow: Opening}
{key: G}
{tempo: 115}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Hymnbook (Richmond, Virginia: Presbyterian Church in the United States, 1955), # 207)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Welcome, [D]hap[G]py [C]morn[G]ing!
[Am]Age to age [D]shall [G]say:
[G]Hell to[C]day is [D7]van[G]quished,
[D]Heav’n [G]is [D]won__[A7]__ to[D]day!
[Bm]Lo! the [F#7]dead is [Bm]living,
[G]God forever[Bm]more!
[Em]Him, their [F#m]true cre[D]ator,
[D]All [G]His [D]works__[A7]__ ad[D]ore!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Welcome, [C]happy [G]morn[D7]ing!
[Em]Age to [G]age__[D7]__ shall [G]say.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Earth her [D]joy [G]con[C]fess[G]es,
[Am]Clothing her [D]for [G]spring,
[G]All fresh [C]gifts re[D7]turned [G]with
[D]Her [G]re[D]turn__[A7]__ing [D]king:
[Bm]Bloom in [F#7]every [Bm]meadow,
[G]Leaves on every [Bm]bough,
[Em]Speak His [F#m]sorrow [D]ended,
[D]Hail [G]His [D]tri__[A7]__umph [D]now.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Months in [D]due [G]suc[C]cession,
[G]Days [Am]of lengthen[D]ing [G]light,
[G]Hours and [C]passing [D7]mo[G]ments
[D]Praise [G]Thee [D]in__[A7]__ their [D]flight.
[Bm]Brightness [F#7]of the [Bm]morning,
[G]Sky and fields and [Bm]sea,
[Em]Vanquis[F#m]her of [D]darkness,
[D]Bring [G]their [D]praise__[A7]__ to [D]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
[G]Loose the [D]souls [G]long [C]pri[G]soned,
[Am]Bound with Sa[D]tan’s [G]chain;
[G]All that [C]now is [D7]fall[G]en
[D]Raise [G]to [D]life__[A7]__ a[D]gain;
[Bm]Show Thy [F#7]face in [Bm]brightness,
[G]Bid the nations [Bm]see;
[Em]Bring a[F#m]gain our [D]daylight:
[D]Day [G]re[D]turns__[A7]__ with [D]Thee!
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
